// A minimal carrier of the "another creature you control" filtered-subject
// shape (`And([Creature, Not(Ref(This)), ControlledBy(Ref(You))])`, the
// OtherCreatureYouControl atom) on BOTH a "dies" (ZoneChange to graveyard)
// and a general leaves-the-battlefield ([CR#603.6c]) event trigger — no
// canon-slice card triggers off a qualified (non-bare) subject for either
// event, so this fixture isolates the shared subject-phrase qualifier walk
// (fragment.rs's subject_phrase) across both event_clause arms that call
// ability::subject_of. Oracle-equivalent: "Whenever another creature you
// control dies, you gain 1 life." / "Whenever another creature you control
// leaves the battlefield, you gain 1 life."
Normal(
    name: "Filtered Subject Triggers",
    mana_cost: [Generic(2), Black],
    types: [Enchantment],
    abilities: [
        Triggered(event: Dies(OtherCreatureYouControl), effect: ChangeLife(You, Up(1))),
        Triggered(event: LeavesBattlefield(OtherCreatureYouControl), effect: ChangeLife(You, Up(1))),
    ],
)
